module tasks.`2026-11-20-seat-close-grace-never-finalizes`

task SeatCloseGraceNeverFinalizes {
  title "seat_close: seats stay closed_grace forever after the 60 s undo deadline, and the call times out with 'UI frame incomplete'"
  verify $ cargo nextest run -p bboxy450-term-mux -E 'test(close)'
  paths "crates/bbt-mux", "crates/bboxy450-term/src"
  brief """
    Our stand: subtract before you add.

    ## Evidence (2026-11-20 16:25, Oracle)
    `seat_list` shows six seats in `closed_grace` with no live process, five past `close.deadline_ms` (ui-kit 01M7T75R..., inbox 01M7T75S..., gate-repairs 01M7TDTG... since 2026-11-19; ui-kit-land 01M7VGHT...; svg 01M7X2RB...). Several `seat_close` calls returned `unavailable: timeout: UI frame incomplete; target=None ... effects=[Lifecycle(Target{...undo:false})=Ok(false)]` yet the seat moved to `closed_grace`.

    ## Do
    Find who finalizes `closed_grace` -> `closed_retained` after the deadline, and why it never runs (likely waits on a UI frame/close control that never completes, or only runs on a UI event). Finalization must be owned by the mux on its own clock, independent of the GUI; the tool reply must report the applied transition instead of a frame timeout once the lifecycle change is recorded. Model the close lifecycle (close, undo inside grace, deadline, GUI absent/restart, process already gone) with a broken control that never finalizes; process witness with no GUI attached.
    ## Evidence added 2026-11-20 18:30 (Oracle)
    - A second `seat_close` on a `closed_grace` seat whose process is gone (ui-kit 01M7T75R..., generation 1) is refused: `rejected: target binding changed before orphan close`; the seat stays `closed_grace`. So no tool path can finalize it; six seats are stuck (ui-kit, inbox 01M7T75S..., gate-repairs 01M7TDTG..., ui-kit-land 01M7VGHT..., svg 01M7X2RB..., inbox 01M7X6CW...), all without processes.
    - Acceptance adds: an orphaned `closed_grace` seat past its deadline finalizes on the mux clock, and a repeated `seat_close` on it is idempotent (reports the finalized state) instead of refusing.
    """

  managed {
    authorship = json"{\"kind\":\"seat\",\"process_generation\":\"1\",\"public_key\":\"rYfaNArK5+cM3H57EoxFBlfNLEqHQzRISfRoopxCK5A=\",\"signer\":\"seat:01M7VC8EK2C7DQXBNCE9V0J0MH\"}"
    created = json"\"2026-11-21T00:15:45.949Z\""
    created_by = json"\"seat:01M7VC8EK2C7DQXBNCE9V0J0MH\""
    delegated_by = json"\"seat:01M7VC8EK2C7DQXBNCE9V0J0MH\""
    id = json"\"01M7XQB157XPJ959B2FG7CKR44\""
